{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And now it was not you, etc.</b> Meaning, to give a reason to remove from their hearts the suspicion of hatred, lest they think that Joseph would harbor hatred against them and hate them for having acted cruelly toward him, and it would seem farfetched in their eyes that Joseph's heart could be whole with them. Therefore he said to them: It is true that at the time of the deed, when they sold him, the matter was alien in his eyes — how could there be such cruelty in the hearts of brothers toward their brother? — and they are fitting to be hated by him." "<b>But now</b>, after seeing all that resulted from his descent to Egypt, he knew that the deed was from HaShem, and they performed His mission, blessed be He, and not a mission of their own. And in this there is no room to harbor enmity against them, nor to withhold the quality of brotherhood from them." "<b>Or perhaps</b> — for in this they would have no face to stand before their father when the matter was revealed, since they were the ones who caused him mourning and weeping for twenty-two years, and they did the wondrous deed in selling their brother. And it appears to me that they would not even be ashamed before their father. And it might have been said that Jacob did not know the substance of the deed, but this is a farfetched path, for it is obvious that he would not refrain from investigating how matters unfolded until Joseph went down to Egypt — and also the matter of the ketonet hapasim (ornamented tunic) brought to him dipped in blood. Rather, certainly through the argument of ״לֹא אַתֶּם שְׁלַחְתֶּם״ etc. (״it was not you who sent me״) that Joseph stated, the matter was recognized that this was from HaShem, and there is no room to question His ways. And this is what they said, of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 87:1): ״Jacob deserved to go down in chains, etc.״"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:53.984901667Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}